{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/142813-my-impression-on-the-celestial-bureaucracy","id":142813,"title":"My impression on the Celestial Bureaucracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-19T17:29:23-07:00","id":142813,"title":"My impression on the Celestial Bureaucracy","content":"Just finished reading the part of the Celestial Bureaucracy in Scion: Companion and I'm conflicted. The structure is nice I especially like the write-up on Sun Wukong. And yet, the goal of most of the pantheon consists of wanting complete domination of all three Worlds: (Overworld, Underworld, and the Mortal World), especially the Yellow Emperor. I know that the pantheons only work together because of the threat of the Titans, but the write-up for first edition makes it seem to me that most of the Celestial Bureaucracy are nothing but mustache-twirling Snidley Whiplashes. I know that the Bureacracy believe that the other pantheons are &quot;barbaric&quot;, but this prejudice just makes them douchy as a result. This is compounded by the most powerful ability of Taiyi, which is Reshape Shen. With that, a Bureaucrat can literally convert a God from a different pantheon to their side without their knowledge, something that can only be reversed by the Wyrd Avatar.<br /> <br /> This concerns me because this gives me the idea that the Celestial Bureaucracy may have secretly caused the Fall of Atlantis, setting the other pantheons upon them with their &quot;barbarian vs barbarian&quot; strategy, then use Reshape Shen to make them Chinese. I know that this is optional, but the prospect of it just scares me.<br /> <br /> I hope that the Celestial Bureaucracy write-up for 2E makes them less like douchebags because as a pantheon, they should be better than this. Just saying.<br /> <br /> Am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T17:54:08-07:00","id":142832,"title":"","content":"Pretty much every culture believes that every other culture is barbaric and uncivilized. For reference, check any point in history where two cultures collide. There are some outstanding counter-examples, like how the Romans loved Ancient Greece (but thought that current Greeks were a bunch of hicks), but generally that's not the rule. Are the Shen douchey? Yeah, but so is everyone else. How should they be &quot;better&quot;? The Aztecs, Greeks and Japanese certainly aren't friendly to outsiders. It'd be a stretch to say <i>any</i> of the Pantheons are &quot;friendly&quot; to outsides, but some are slightly less xenophobic.<br /> <br /> Taiyi is just a mess full of mismatched powers cobbled together from an assortment of myths and cultural traditions. It has no unity, theme or cohesion. It's one of the less well-written PSPs, especially because of Reshape Shen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T22:08:57-07:00","id":143072,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but with every other pantheon, they are subtle about it. In fact, part 4, which deals with Divine Politics, tells us what the pantheons think of each other. The blatant RAW about their utter distaste for anything non-Chinese and the fact that their most powerful ability basically brainwashes Gods mind, body, and soul, is about as subtle as a Mack truck through a brick wall. I hope that Onyx Path ramps up the subtlety in 2E so that the intent isn't quite so pronounced as it was here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T00:52:44-07:00","id":143178,"title":"","content":"Most PSP are somewhat powerful. In fact, you can also say that Gods could turn into his Avatar forms just to do whatever they want. The thing is they won't because they are Gods and they have other things to handle than reshaping anyone just like that, especially Chinese people. Major decisions are never taken lightly just because they want to. No God is brave/ outrageous/ foolish enough to do such things without thinking about the consequences. It's just as powerful for a nation that can be destroyed by a nuclear bomb. It's cheating to have such a powerful weapon against any country but no one would dare to use it unless there is an emergency that forces one to do it.<br /> <br /> The Chinese PSP can be powerful, I don't care. What irritates me is what Telgar says: no cohesion. Nothing seems linked in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T10:09:58-07:00","id":143637,"title":"","content":"Imagine the paperwork it would take to get authorization to reshape a barbaric god into a civilized one. Then imagine how much paperwork you would have to fill out for an UNauthorized transformation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T18:19:43-07:00","id":146232,"title":"","content":"unauthorized is faster! Approving is what takes longer... that's why Sun Wukong ans Nezha exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T07:32:14-07:00","id":146716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/142813-my-impression-on-the-celestial-bureaucracy?p=146232#post146232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unauthorized is faster! Approving is what takes longer... that's why Sun Wukong ans Nezha exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great IF you're them. Neither one of them was a Scion (magical beastie or puddle of goo...). Unless they're you're pa and they LIKE you and want to run interference, you're stuck in the bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> In fact, as persnickity as the Monkey King has gotten about his position and titles, I bet he's ALL OVER having his children behave appropriately (at least while under the Eye of Heaven). Ne zha probably could care less. But he probably won't help. (In our game with a Scion of Ne Zha, any meeting with him usually involved getting the crap beaten out of him.)<br /> <br /> &quot;Here is your form for being the child of an unruly god begging leave of the Celestial Emperor for the right to file petitions before his Court. That will require you to use your seal. You don't have a seal? Here is the paperwork to request the paperwork for a seal. It includes the place to write your apology for not having had this done already. Please compose it in the form of the poem of three verses, praising the three worlds and the five directions and include references to the benevolence of the Celestial Dragon and Phoenix. Sarcasm will not be tolerated and will expiated by a day and night in the Hell of a Thousand Knives...&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T08:12:58-07:00","id":146750,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think the Celestial Bureaucracy writeup over-stressed the bureaucracy part.<br /> <br /> If you're a Chinese Scion, you're probably not going to start out with your own position in the bureaucracy. Instead, you're probably one of your patron's retainers, which can mean either lots or next to no leeway depending on your patron. Someone like Hou Yi is probably going to keep a very close eye on his Scions, but the same can't be said of Erlang Shen. In my opinion, there isn't much evidence that Chinese Scions should be forced to serve within the system, not least because half of the big names are pseudo-hermits living on their private mountains with their personal retainers.<br /> <br /> And before someone points out how Heaven set out to subdue Sun Wukong, he started it by extorting one of the Dragon Kings and <i>making all of his monkeys immortal by threatening the Ten Yama Kings</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T16:35:10-07:00","id":147275,"title":"","content":"After having to translate the examinations for the lowest levels of Ming era examinations, I'm UNDER-stating the level of bureaucracy of earthly China. The Shen have never had a Dynastic collapse, intermediate period, etc. The bureaucracy would have flowered like and endlessly fractal perfect lotus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T19:24:31-07:00","id":148335,"title":"","content":"I know how excruciating the imperial examinations were supposed to have been, but I'm not seeing the connections between said examinations and the reach of the Chinese bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> Regardless, if we're taking Fengshen Yanyi into account, then the celestial bureaucracy would've been established at the founding of the Zhou dynasty. Starting out, it would've had to contend with the entrenched influence of big names such as Fuxi, Nuwa, and Shennong, much as how the earthly dynasties had to contend with the influence of the elite in each province of the empire. It's possible that the celestial bureaucracy could've spread to swallow all other sources of power in the society of Chinese immortals, but if we're using Xiyouji, this is clearly not the case. Some of the immortals serve as officials in the celestial bureaucracy, while other immortals live separately but not necessarily in opposition to the central power of the Jade Emperor.<br /> <br /> In my mind, cramming all of the Chinese immortals into the celestial bureaucracy would fly in the face of the Chinese tradition of hermits cultivating themselves in seclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T20:31:54-07:00","id":148358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/142813-my-impression-on-the-celestial-bureaucracy?p=148335#post148335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my mind, cramming all of the Chinese immortals into the celestial bureaucracy would fly in the face of the Chinese tradition of hermits cultivating themselves in seclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chinese had absolutely no issues with the tradition of hermits being a part of the fabric of existence that harmonized with the bureaucracy. When the world is righteous, ALL is a reflection of the perfection of Heaven. Hermits cultivating themselves have their place and it is not OUTSIDE the Mandate of Heaven. It's an integral part, in all its many manifestations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T07:39:38-07:00","id":148688,"title":"","content":"I do think that portrayals of the Celestial Bureaucracy are often putting the cart before the horse. Unless there's a Titan of Paperwork out there, the bureaucracy was created by the gods at some point, likely as a convenience for those in power, likely because running the universe is hard work even for a god. But since there's very little turnover in the leadership and we're talking about gods who can lay waste to large nations in an afternoon, the idea of them being bound by paperwork seems farcical to me.<br /> <br /> The amount to which the Bureaucracy interferes annoyingly with the lives of any god ought represent the degree to which the people who outrank them dislike them. If you're a scion whose parent likes you, then all the little functionaries ought be currying your favor, or at least not giving you shit about stamping forms in triplicate. If they dislike you, though, then they can start turning the screws.<br /> <br /> The real great powers of the Bureaucracy ought be beyond its little annoyances. When Guan Yin makes a move, no functionary is going to be dumb enough to get in her way. Instead, there ought be a whole department just for &quot;making sure the greatest gods aren't inconvenienced in the slightest.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3120-spider-ham","name":"Spider Ham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:55:57-07:00","id":148749,"title":"","content":"Are you averring that the Emperor of Heaven exercises no control over the other Legend 12 gods due to his position? That they can do whatever, whenever they want and there is no accountability? That certainly isn't the way the Chinese perceive the universal order to function. <br /> <br /> Sure, Ne zha and the Monkey King are running around being BAD BOYS, but they do suffer some penalties in that regard (mostly did for the Monkey King, but still does to a degree). By choosing to stand outside the Celestial order, they are at a disadvantage when they would otherwise like to utilize it. Plus they have to crash all the best parties, because they will never get invites. Or they'll get invited and the whole party will be boring and un-fun because they are making everyone uncomfortable. (Susanoo gets the same status among the Kami.)<br /> <br /> Guan yin (and probably the other Legend 12 deities with the notable exceptions) is at the level where, when she craved audience with the Emperor, he almost always grants it and does so with a minimum of fuss. Chinese Emperors certainly had levels of officials that had this kind of clout. She doesn't have to fill out reams of paperwork. She has the prerogatives of her position. <br /> <br /> PC Scion don't have this kind of clout. And they don't have the history that lets the celestial bad boys get away with their antics. If they don't play the bureaucratic game, they are going to be in significant amounts of trouble. <br /> <br /> Though I do love the idea of of a Department of &quot;Sweeping the Leaves from the Paths of the Most Divine&quot; . I can imagine how PC Scions would run afoul of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T21:56:11-07:00","id":149139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/142813-my-impression-on-the-celestial-bureaucracy?p=148358#post148358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chinese had absolutely no issues with the tradition of hermits being a part of the fabric of existence that harmonized with the bureaucracy. When the world is righteous, ALL is a reflection of the perfection of Heaven. Hermits cultivating themselves have their place and it is not OUTSIDE the Mandate of Heaven. It's an integral part, in all its many manifestations.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I see it, the hermits are part of the society of Chinese immortals but not part of the celestial bureaucracy that regulates them. Unless you're an official of the celestial bureaucracy, you're bound by the rules of the society of Chinese immortals, but you're not at the celestial bureaucracy's complete beck and call because you're a civilian. You can still be called up to serve the celestial bureaucracy because the Jade Emperor is your ruler, but barring exceptional circumstances, the celestial bureaucracy should be no more controlling than most of its earthly counterparts and probably less so than a great many of them.<br /> <br /> That said, I can see the celestial bureaucracy taking much more interest in Chinese Scions than most immortals, since having kids is probably not on the list of approved ways in which humans and immortals can interact. Though this should be counterbalanced somewhat by the fact that most Chinese Scions will have powerful patrons to serve in the celestial bureaucracy's stead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T03:53:48-07:00","id":149300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/142813-my-impression-on-the-celestial-bureaucracy?p=148749#post148749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you averring that the Emperor of Heaven exercises no control over the other Legend 12 gods due to his position? That they can do whatever, whenever they want and there is no accountability? That certainly isn't the way the Chinese perceive the universal order to function.<br /> <br /> Sure, Ne zha and the Monkey King are running around being BAD BOYS, but they do suffer some penalties in that regard (mostly did for the Monkey King, but still does to a degree). By choosing to stand outside the Celestial order, they are at a disadvantage when they would otherwise like to utilize it. Plus they have to crash all the best parties, because they will never get invites. Or they'll get invited and the whole party will be boring and un-fun because they are making everyone uncomfortable. (Susanoo gets the same status among the Kami.)<br /> <br /> Guan yin (and probably the other Legend 12 deities with the notable exceptions) is at the level where, when she craved audience with the Emperor, he almost always grants it and does so with a minimum of fuss. Chinese Emperors certainly had levels of officials that had this kind of clout. She doesn't have to fill out reams of paperwork. She has the prerogatives of her position.<br /> <br /> PC Scion don't have this kind of clout. And they don't have the history that lets the celestial bad boys get away with their antics. If they don't play the bureaucratic game, they are going to be in significant amounts of trouble.<br /> <br /> Though I do love the idea of of a Department of &quot;Sweeping the Leaves from the Paths of the Most Divine&quot; . I can imagine how PC Scions would run afoul of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I'm not saying that the Emperor has no power, or that gods can do WHATEVER they want, but I see it as a sort of gentleman's agreement between the greatest gods. They like the bureaucracy because it enforces modes of behavior that suit them. They generally like the ceremony and the underlings. But I don't think that they would want to see themselves or their favored children stymied by the bureaucracy purely for form's sake.<br /> <br /> A good example would be Monkey. Monkey could defeat every Shen in the universe with one hand tied behind his back, but none of it would matter, because he would never get the one thing he craved from them: respect. That didn't come until Xuanzang came along and taught him how to moderate his behavior. When he could do that, he was accepted as one of them. The books imply that he's still something of a roustabout, but the gods are willing to tolerate him because he generally displays respect for the hierarchy and process. No one's going to give him shit about dotting every I and crossing every T so long as he keeps that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3120-spider-ham","name":"Spider Ham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T08:51:44-07:00","id":149421,"title":"","content":"That is definitely a very non-Chinese way of viewing the Chinese pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}